==French==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Fr-faute.ogg|audio|lang=fr}}
* {{IPA|/fot/|lang=fr}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|faute}}, from {{etyl|VL.|fr}} {{m|la|*fallita}}, feminine of *''fallitus'', in place of {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|falsus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|fallō}}. Compare Catalan, Spanish, and Portuguese {{m|ca|falta}}.

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f}}

# [[error]], [[mistake]]
#: ''une faute d'orthographe'' - a spelling mistake
# [[fault]], [[blame]]
#: ''c'est de ma faute'' - it's my fault / I'm to blame
#: ''c'est toujours la faute aux autres'' - it's always other people's fault / other people are always to blame
#: ''il [[rejeter|rejette]] la faute sur son patron'' - he laid/put the blame on his boss
# {{lb|fr|legal}} [[wrong]], [[misdemeanor]]
# {{lb|fr|sports}} [[foul]], [[fault]] {{gloss|infraction of the rules}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|fr|faute de}}

